For the attraction power, if there's a magnet in cell $i$ and an iron in cell $j$, the power is $P_{i,j} = K+1 - |j-i| - S_{i,j}$. Here, $S_{i,j}$ is the number of sheets between cells $i$ and $j$. If there are no sheets, it’s zero. If there’s a wall ($X$), the power is zero. If the power is negative or zero, the magnet cannot attract the iron piece.

We’ll use a greedy algorithm to select the magnets that can attract the most iron pieces. We’ll start with the magnet with the highest power and move to the next one if it doesn’t attract any iron. We’ll keep track of the magnets we’ve chosen to ensure no magnet attracts more than one iron piece.
